-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Nightshade
  Publisher   Ultimate Play The Game, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Nightshade (1985)(Ultimate Play The Game)[a][a].z80
  MD5         7b4e8280896d7ff34b93e83ddba9d01c

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Every figure painted by its parts, following the drawn lines:
              the hero in a grey mail hood and collar, skin face, arms and
              legs, a leather belt and boots, and his tunic in his health
              colour (white, yellow, then green); monsters, bosses and items
              in their own colours. No white outlines or edges. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Jon Attree.

  Pace        original (+0.05% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same start
              state; probe 0xDA7A, keys given after the update's last read
              (0xE32B), R fixed at 4 sites in both games; game state, 90
              addresses, equal at every update)

  Changes     1.1: the game now holds the original's pace; 1.0 ran up to 8.7%
              slow in short busy stretches.

  Note        Default and Enhanced colours both play at the original's pace in
              JNext, 2026-11-08, same input and game state equal at every
              update, 4 runs each: default overall 0.0 to +0.1%, quiet -0.1 to
              +0.2%, busy -0.1 to +0.1%; Enhanced overall 0.0 to +0.7%, quiet
              -0.1 to +0.8%, busy +0.1 to +0.5% (1.0, same measure: overall up
              to +1.9%, quiet up to +2.5%). The CPU speed in use is kept as
              the base; the game's own code runs at 7 MHz for short spells to
              win back time, and sound stays on the base clock. Known issues:
              slowest stretch of 20 updates +1.4% default, +1.9% Enhanced
              (1.0: +7.1%, +8.7%). Missing: not reached in testing: building
              interiors, the four weapons, the bosses and the end (their
              Enhanced colours seen only on sheets); hardware untested.

